  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Morocco &#x2013; Textile Products for Healthcare and Medical sector</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With a guarantee from DGGF to support Rabobank&#x2019;s loan to Skylla Europe B.V. (Skylla), Skylla will be able to establish a new production facility for medical textile production in Morocco. Skylla is specialized in the development, production and distribution (supply chain management) of textile products for the healthcare and medical sector. They already have production facilities in Tunisia and North Macedonia and will establish the a new production facility in Morocco. The investment will contribute to the creation of approximately 350 new jobs, mainly women. In terms of human resources, they plan to replicate the HR practices from their other facilities, ensuring compliance with the SA 8000 Social Accountability standard, and place significant importance on Living Wage (LW) principles. Also the company is committed to sustainability, with all its branches adhering to strict sustainability goals. They actively pursue eco-friendly operations, such as reusing packaging and transportation waste. Besides that they hold various ISO certifications focused on sustainability and environmental management. Finally this investment will create a positive impact on the Dutch economy. On the one hand this gives the company the possibility to grow in turnover and profit, and on the other hand most likely a couple of new jobs will be created.</narrative>
  </description>
